    "summary": "Adire: a single panel of imported European white calico cotton, dyed in indigo in Nigeria using stitch resist and tie dye methods. The central pattern is in stitch-resist using raffia, and has broad lines obliquely across the cloth; the ends have small tie-dyed circles. The pattern name was recorded by W.B.Fagg as Ọlọwọ odi (=&#039;left hand&#039;).",
